# Water Motion Architecture (AI)

Before implementing any feature, read:

`docs/WATER_MOTION_ARCHITECTURE_GUIDE.md`

First responsibility is **understand architecture**, not write code.

## Domain ownership

- **Case** = aggregate root (workflow, booking, offer, feedback, report, notifications ops)
- **Customer** = identity layer only (incremental migration; Case references Customer)
- Never move Offer / Workflow / Feedback / Reports under Customer

## Protected contracts (no break without explicit approval)

- `POST /api/cases`, `GET /api/public/water-check-offer`
- Dashboard payloads, Framer payloads, LINE webhook envelope
- Notion property names (never rename/remove)

## Matching

Exact match only. Normalize phone/email. **No fuzzy. No name auto-merge.**

## Forbidden unless explicitly instructed

Rewrite Booking/Workflow/Offer; rename APIs/routes/Notion props; fuzzy matching; break Dashboard/Framer/LINE; redesign architecture; unrelated refactors.

## Every implementation must report

Architecture understanding, plan, affected modules, compatibility, regression, migration impact, performance, rollback, verification.

